.MARINE...
(Tonight through next Saturday)
Issued at 239 PM PST Mon Nov 2 2026

Seas will continue to build across the outer waters tonight
through Wednesday morning, becoming rough and bringing hazardous
conditions for small craft. Gentle to moderate northwesterly
breezes will increase and back tonight to become moderate to fresh
southwesterly breezes ahead of an approaching cold front. Rain
moves in Tuesday with this system, bringing with it a 15-20%
chance of thunderstorms north of Pigeon Point. Moderate to fresh
northerly breezes and moderate to rough seas will prevail
Wednesday through Friday.

